#
# N3 - a prescription version with no content address. Immutability is enforced by
# content addressing rather than a flag, so an unaddressed version makes in-place
# revision undetectable. MUST trip logic:PrescriptionVersionIsContentAddressedConstraint.
# NOT logic:PrescriptionVersionImmutabilityConstraint: that law compares the version's
# current address with what a run froze, and its guard binds both, so an unaddressed
# version falls outside it. The overwrite is
# prescription-version-revised-under-a-running-enactment.ttl.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/logic/tests/> .

ex:versionNoDigest a logic:PrescriptionVersion ;
    rdfs:label "a prescription version that is not content-addressed"@en .
